  correct: 1,
  explanation: "CIN is the energy that must be overcome to initiate convection. A strong CIN cap suppresses convective development even when CAPE is high \u2014 this is why some high-CAPE days are convectively inactive. When sufficient forcing (solar heating, frontal lifting) overcomes the cap, the stored CAPE produces explosive convective development.",
