  explanation: "Ice crystal icing (ICI) is an engine hazard, not a structural one. Dry ice crystals do not accumulate on airfoils but can enter engine inlets, partially melt on warm compressor blades, and re-freeze further downstream \u2014 restricting flow passages or causing stalls. Responsible for numerous engine power loss events in high-altitude convective clouds (cirrus, CB anvils).",
  reference: "Bob Tait CPL Meteorology",
