  correct: 2,
  explanation: "Glaciation is the conversion of supercooled liquid water droplets to ice crystals. It occurs between approximately \u221210\u00b0C and \u221240\u00b0C \u2014 the exact temperature depends on droplet size and presence of ice nuclei. Below the glaciation level (warmer temperatures), SLW is abundant. Above it, ice crystals dominate and SLW is rare.",
